# Requirements

## Hypotheses

### H1: Single channel sine drive moves the body

WHEN one control channel (c0) is driven by a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1 and the other four are zero, THE system SHALL end with a net x displacement smaller than 0.3 m.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [-0.3, 0.3]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1.0
ch = 0
freq = 1.0
```

### H2: c3 or c4 alone produce net forward crawl

WHEN c3 alone is driven by a 1 Hz sine of amplitude 1, THE system SHALL end with a net x displacement above 0.1 m.

```prediction
# relies on: E1
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 0.6]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1.0
ch = 3
freq = 1.0
```

### H3: Constant c0/c1 act as enable or gain for the sine-driven channels

WHEN c0 and c1 are held at 1 while c2, c3 and c4 carry a 1 Hz sine, THE system SHALL end with a net x displacement above 0.1 m.

```prediction
# relies on: E1, E2
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 0.6]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1.0
ch = 6
freq = 1.0
```

### H4: A quarter-cycle phase offset between c3 and c4 produces forward crawl

WHEN c3 is a 1 Hz sine and c4 leads it by 90 degrees with c0, c1 and c2 at zero, THE system SHALL end with x between 0.1 and 0.6 m and heading within 30 degrees of zero.

```prediction
